      "assistant_text": "The **[[write-journal]]** page describes how Grimoire\u0027s guarded write path maintains reliability through journaling:\n\nBefore any file is overwritten, the system records its prior state \u2014 either the file\u0027s existing content or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist yet \u2014 into an in-memory write journal. This acts as a transaction log. If the agent run fails for any reason (turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every write in reverse order: restoring original content to files that already existed and deleting newly created files. This mechanism provides all-or-nothing semantics for file writes without needing a database transaction.\n\nThe page notes that the Query agent never triggers the rollback path since it has no write capability at all, though the journal infrastructure is shared across the agent runtime library.",
